    pr_ref:  # 8d7d
    description: "Git submodules become installed-dependency source (ADR-0004 point 1 row, amendment item): skipped by default, disclosed, opt-in via --trace-deps <path> / trace_deps (so the results-cache key already covers it).\n\nDetection by evidence, not name: a directory listed in .gitmodules whose HEAD entry is a gitlink (mode 160000), read with the same `git ls-tree HEAD -- <dir>` call discovery._head_entries already trusts (never the index -- the core.fsmonitor hazard point 3 documents). Outside git or with no commits: .gitmodules entry plus a `.git` FILE inside the directory. Add an entry to discovery.INSTALLED_DEP_RULES; extend the installed_deps disclosure (\"... git submodule ...\").\n\nTest with a fixture (the corpus cannot measure it: 35 repos, 362 submodule paths, 0 populated on 2026-10-15): populated submodule skipped and disclosed; --trace-deps <path> analyses it as tier 3; an unpopulated submodule path is a no-op."  # 8d7d
    fields: {}  # 8d7d
